@page "/mentor/tasks"
@layout AppLayout
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = Roles.Mentor + "," + Roles.Admin + "," + Roles.Staff)]
@namespace AuthWithAdmin.Client.Pages.Mentor
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Components
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Services
@using AuthWithAdmin.Shared.AuthSharedModels
@inject IMentorWorkspaceService Workspace
@inject IPersonalTasksService PersonalTasks
@inject NavigationManager Nav
@implements IDisposable

@*
    ── המשימות שלי — the mentor's unified work queue ────────────────────────
    Visual source:   Motiva Mentor Tasks.dc.html, in the Claude Design project
                     "Motiva visual language exploration".
    Component source: the finalized Student experience — every surface below is
                     a shared M* primitive under `.motiva-final`, not a mentor
                     copy of one.
    Data source:     IMentorWorkspaceService.

    THE POINT OF THE PAGE
    A student's "המשימות שלי" is a list of assigned project tasks. A mentor's
    is three different feeds that happen to share one question — what needs me
    — so the page is a queue, not a list:

        הגשות לבדיקה           GET api/mentor/attention  (Kind = Submission)
        בקשות הדורשות פעולה     GET api/mentor/attention  (Kind = Request)
        משימות אישיות           GET api/projects/personal-tasks

    WHERE THE URGENCY COMES FROM
    The first two feeds arrive already filtered, aged and ordered worst-first
    (NEEDS ATTENTION → WAITING → NEW, oldest first inside each band). This page
    holds no status filter, no day arithmetic and no threshold: it used to carry
    two different magic numbers for one idea — a review escalated at 4 days, a
    request at 3 — and both are now the single server-side
    MentorAttention.AttentionThresholdDays, which the daily digest reads too.

    NEEDS ATTENTION IS THE ONLY STATE THAT ESCALATES VISUALLY. An item that
    arrived today reads calmly on purpose: there is no deadline in this product,
    so nothing is late and "new" is not an alarm.

    "משימות באיחור" MEANS PERSONAL TASKS, AND ONLY PERSONAL TASKS. They are the
    one kind here that carries a real DueDate the mentor set, so they are the one
    kind that may legitimately read as באיחור.

    ── THE FILTER IS THE DESIGN'S PILL GROUP, NOT A KPI ROW ─────────────────
    The reference puts four tabs in one segmented pill group at the reading end
    of the TITLE ROW — הכל · ממתינות לבדיקתך② · … — and has no KPI cards on
    this screen at all. This page used four MKpiCards for the same job, so the
    switch is a change of shape, not of behaviour:

      * the three filters are unchanged (Reviews / Requests / Personal) and so
        is the ?focus= vocabulary that deep-links into them from בית;
      * every count the KPI row carried survives — three of them ride their own
        tab as a badge, and משימות אישיות באיחור moves to the rose annotation on
        the משימות אישיות heading, beside the section it was always about;
      * the removable "מציג: …" chip is gone. With a real "הכל" tab, the active
        pill IS the indicator, and the chip restated it a second time.

    Clicking a tab selects; clicking "הכל" clears. (The KPI cards toggled off on
    a second click — a tab group must not, or the page would end up with no tab
    lit and no way to tell why the list is complete.)

    ── THE ROW CARRIES FOUR THINGS, AND NOTHING ELSE ─────────────────────────
    The reference's collapsed row is a dot, a title, one short line naming the
    team, and one short state phrase. That is the whole row, in all three
    sections, which is what lets three different feeds be scanned as one queue.

    This page had grown a row that stated far more than a scan needs — the
    project AND the team AND the milestone AND who submitted it, over a full
    sentence of waiting age. Every one of those facts is real and every one of
    them still exists; what changed is where they are read. The list answers
    "what is here and how long has it waited"; the submission drawer, the
    request modal and the task editor answer everything else, and each row is
    already a deep link to exactly the one that owns it.

    So the collapsed row now shows:
      * the title, unchanged;
      * ONE short label for the team — TeamName, falling back to the project
        only when a team name is missing. Project titles in this product are
        long ("Motiva — Final Project Management Platform") and the team name
        is the thing a mentor recognises;
      * MentorAging.ShortLabel — "ממתינה 5 ימים", not "ממתינה לבדיקה כבר 5
        ימים". The long phrase is still what the detail surfaces and the daily
        digest print, because it is still the same WaitingLabel;
      * the status dot, unchanged.

    Dropped from the row, not from the model: the milestone, the submitter, the
    request type (the title already names it) and the trailing chevron — a
    decoration on a row that is already a link.

    The escalation still reaches a screen reader in words: MentorAging's
    "דורש תשומת לב" is folded into each escalated row's accessible name, so the
    meaning is never carried by the rose alone.

    ── SECTION HEADINGS ARE THE REFERENCE'S COLOURED GROUP LABELS ────────────
    15px/700 with .03em tracking in the section's own semantic role — blue for
    what is waiting on a review, violet for what is waiting on a decision, quiet
    ink for the mentor's own list. Still the shared MSectionHeading, so the row
    layout, the "לכל הבקשות" link and the trailing slot are the component's; only
    the label's size and colour are re-based, in this page's stylesheet.

    The count that rode each heading is gone: the same three numbers are on the
    filter tabs one row above, and stating them twice is exactly the density
    this pass removes.

    WHAT IS NOT HERE, AND WHY
      * The reference's expand-in-place card, with אישור והעברה למרצה /
        החזרה לתיקון on the row. A mentor has no approve-or-return endpoint for
        a submission — their only decision endpoint is the extension
        recommendation — so those two buttons would be controls that cannot
        work. Rows keep the navigation contract they have always had: a
        submission opens its project, a request opens MentorRequestModal.
      * Generic אישור / דחייה on any request row; see MentorRequestModal.
*@

<div class="mt-header-bleed">
    <MPageHeader Variant="MPageHeader.HeaderVariant.Compact"
                 Title="המשימות שלי"
                 Subtitle="הגשות, בקשות ותזכורות אישיות שממתינות לפעולה שלך.">
        @* The reference puts the switcher on the title row, pushed to the
           reading end — not on a full-width row of its own. *@
        <Actions>
            @if (!_loading)
            {
                <MFilterTabs Tabs="@FilterTabs"
                             ActiveKey="@ActiveTabKey"
                             OnSelect="SelectFocus"
                             AriaLabel="סינון תור העבודה" />
            }
        </Actions>
    </MPageHeader>
</div>

<div class="mt-body">

    @if (_loading)
    {
        <MLoadingState Label="טוענת את המשימות…" />
    }
    else
    {
        @*
            ── The workspace ────────────────────────────────────────────────
            ONE row that fills what is left of the viewport, not three
            sections laid down the page. The composition is the finalized
            Student Tasks screen's, lifted whole (StudentTasksPage.razor.css):
            a two-column stretch row, both columns sharing a top and a bottom
            edge, every panel scrolling inside itself and the page not
            scrolling at all.

            Reading start (the wide column) carries the INCOMING queue — what
            teams have sent this mentor and are waiting on: הגשות לבדיקה over
            בקשות הדורשות פעולה. They are two views of the same obligation, so
            they share a column exactly as דורש התייחסות shares one with
            משימות הפרויקט on the student screen.

            The rail carries משימות אישיות, full height. A different KIND of
            work — the mentor's own, self-created and checkable, answering to
            nobody's deadline but theirs — which is why it is a column of its
            own rather than a third block in the stack, and why it is full
            height rather than content height: a panel that stops halfway down
            the row is what made it read as an afterthought.
        *@
        <div class="mt-workspace @WorkspaceClass">

            @if (ShowsPrimary)
            {
                <div class="mt-primary">
                @* ── 1. הגשות לבדיקה ── *@
                @if (Shows(Section.Reviews))
                {
                    <section id="reviews" class="mt-pane @QuietWhenEmpty(_reviews.Count)">
                        <MCard Padding="MCard.CardPadding.None" Fill="true">
                            <div class="mt-card">
                                <div class="mt-card-head">
                                    <MSectionHeading Class="mt-head mt-head-blue" Text="הגשות לבדיקה" />
                                </div>

                                <MScrollArea Tabbable="false">

                                    @if (_reviews.Count == 0)
                                    {
                                        <MEmptyState Title="אין הגשות לבדיקה כרגע."
                                                     Description="כשצוות יגיש תוצר לאבן דרך, הוא יופיע כאן."
                                                     Class="mt-empty" />
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <MRowList AriaLabel="הגשות לבדיקה">
                                            @foreach (var r in _reviews)
                                            {
                                                <MRow Href="@r.Href"
                                                      Primary="@r.Title"
                                                      Secondary="@TeamLabel(r)"
                                                      Status="@TimeChip(r)"
                                                      AriaLabel="@RowAriaLabel(r, $"פתיחת ההגשה {r.Title}")">
                                                    <Leading>
                                                        <MStatusBar Tone="@BarToneFor(r)" />
                                                    </Leading>
                                                </MRow>
                                            }
                                        </MRowList>
                                    }
                                </MScrollArea>
                            </div>
                        </MCard>
                    </section>
                }

                @* ── 2. בקשות הדורשות פעולה ── *@
                @if (Shows(Section.Requests))
                {
                    <section id="requests" class="mt-pane @QuietWhenEmpty(_awaitingMe.Count)">
                        <MCard Padding="MCard.CardPadding.None" Fill="true">
                            <div class="mt-card">
                                <div class="mt-card-head">
                                    <MSectionHeading Class="mt-head mt-head-violet" Text="בקשות הדורשות פעולה"
                                                     LinkHref="/mentor-requests" LinkText="לכל הבקשות" />
                                </div>

                                <MScrollArea Tabbable="false">

                                    @if (_awaitingMe.Count == 0)
                                    {
                                        <MEmptyState Title="אין בקשות שדורשות את תגובתך."
                                                     Description="בקשות שממתינות להמלצתך יופיעו כאן."
                                                     Class="mt-empty" />
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <MRowList AriaLabel="בקשות הדורשות פעולה">
                                            @foreach (var q in _awaitingMe)
                                            {
                                                var id = q.EntityId;
                                                <MRow OnClick="@(() => _openRequestId = id)"
                                                      Primary="@q.Title"
                                                      Secondary="@TeamLabel(q)"
                                                      Status="@TimeChip(q)"
                                                      AriaLabel="@RowAriaLabel(q, $"פתיחת הבקשה {q.Title}")">
                                                    <Leading>
                                                        <MStatusBar Tone="@BarToneFor(q)" />
                                                    </Leading>
                                                </MRow>
                                            }
                                        </MRowList>
                                    }
                                </MScrollArea>
                            </div>
                        </MCard>
                    </section>
                }

                </div>
            }

            @if (Shows(Section.Personal))
            {
                <div class="mt-rail">
                @* ── 3. משימות אישיות ── *@
                <section id="personal" class="mt-pane">
                    <MCard Padding="MCard.CardPadding.None" Fill="true">
                        <div class="mt-card">
                            <div class="mt-card-head">
                                <MSectionHeading Class="mt-head mt-head-quiet" Text="משימות אישיות">
                                    <Trailing>
                                        @* PERSONAL tasks only, and it sits on their own heading.
                                           These carry a real DueDate, so באיחור is a true
                                           statement about them; it would not be about a
                                           submission or a request, neither of which has a
                                           deadline to miss. *@
                                        @if (Counts.PersonalTasksOverdue > 0)
                                        {
                                            <span class="mt-overdue">@Counts.PersonalTasksOverdue באיחור</span>
                                        }
                                        <button type="button" class="mt-add" title="הוספת משימה" aria-label="הוספת משימה"
                                                @onclick="OpenNewTask">
                                            <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                                                 stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true">
                                                <path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"></path>
                                            </svg>
                                        </button>
                                    </Trailing>
                                </MSectionHeading>
                            </div>

                            <MScrollArea Tabbable="false">

                                @if (_visiblePersonal.Count == 0)
                                {
                                    <MEmptyState Title="אין משימות אישיות כרגע."
                                                 Description="תזכורות שתוסיף/י לעצמך יופיעו כאן."
                                                 Class="mt-empty" />
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <MRowList AriaLabel="משימות אישיות">
                                        @foreach (var t in _visiblePersonal)
                                        {
                                            var id = t.Id;
                                            @* One short label for the team, exactly like a submission
                                               or a request row. A task with no project simply has no
                                               second line — "ללא שיוך" is a label for an absence, and the
                                               absence already reads as one. *@
                                            <MRow Class="@(t.IsDone ? "mt-task-done" : null)"
                                                  Secondary="@PersonalTeamLabel(t)"
                                                  Status="@DueChip(t)">
                                                <Leading>
                                                    <button type="button"
                                                            class="mt-check @(t.IsDone ? "mt-check-on" : "")"
                                                            role="checkbox"
                                                            aria-checked="@t.IsDone"
                                                            aria-label="@($"סימון \"{t.Title}\" כהושלמה")"
                                                            disabled="@(_togglingId == id)"
                                                            @onclick="@(() => ToggleTaskAsync(id))">
                                                        @if (t.IsDone)
                                                        {
                                                            <svg width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                                                                 stroke-width="3.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                                                                <path d="m5 13 4.5 4.5L19 7"></path>
                                                            </svg>
                                                        }
                                                    </button>
                                                </Leading>
                                                <PrimaryContent>
                                                    @* The title opens the editor. A personal task is the
                                                       mentor's OWN item, so unlike a submission or a
                                                       request it is editable in place — the checkbox
                                                       stays a separate hit target so completing a task
                                                       never risks opening a dialog. *@
                                                    <button type="button" class="mt-task-title mt-task-edit"
                                                            @onclick="@(() => OpenEditTask(t))"
                                                            aria-label="@($"עריכת \"{t.Title}\"")">
                                                        @t.Title
                                                    </button>
                                                </PrimaryContent>
                                            </MRow>
                                        }
                                    </MRowList>
                                }

                            </MScrollArea>
                            @* Show the toggle whenever the collapsed view is actually
                               hiding something. The old test compared the COMBINED count
                               against the cap, but the collapsed list only ever shows
                               OPEN tasks — so completing the only task left it counted,
                               hidden, and with no control to reveal it. It could then be
                               neither reopened, edited nor deleted. *@
                            @if (_openPersonal.Count > PersonalCollapsedCount || _donePersonal.Count > 0)
                            {
                                <div class="mt-expand">
                                    <button type="button" class="mt-expand-btn" @onclick="TogglePersonalExpanded">
                                        @(_personalExpanded ? "הצג פחות" : "הצג הכל")
                                    </button>
                                </div>
                            }
                        </div>
                    </MCard>
                </section>
                </div>
            }

        </div>
    }
</div>

@* ── Request details, opened in place ── *@
<MentorRequestModal RequestId="@_openRequestId"
                    WaitingLabel="@OpenRequestWaitingLabel"
                    OnClose="@(() => _openRequestId = null)"
                    OnChanged="ReloadAsync" />

@* ── New / edit personal task ──
     The shared component, not an inline copy: /mentor/calendar opens the SAME
     editor, so create, update, delete, validation and the delete confirmation
     exist once. Mirrors how TeamTaskEditModal already serves both the student
     tasks page and the student planner. *@
<MentorPersonalTaskModal IsOpen="@_taskModalOpen"
                         EditingTask="@_editingTask"
                         Projects="@_ws.Projects"
                         OnClose="CloseTaskModal"
                         OnSaved="OnTaskSaved"
                         OnDeleted="OnTaskDeleted" />

@code {
    /// <summary>The three feeds. Also the filter vocabulary — one enum, so a
    /// tab, a section and the ?focus= parameter cannot disagree.</summary>
    private enum Section { Reviews, Requests, Personal }

    private const int PersonalCollapsedCount = 6;

    private MentorWorkspace _ws = MentorWorkspace.Empty;
    private bool _loading = true;

    private IReadOnlyList<MentorAttentionItemDto> _reviews    = Array.Empty<MentorAttentionItemDto>();
    private IReadOnlyList<MentorAttentionItemDto> _awaitingMe = Array.Empty<MentorAttentionItemDto>();
    private List<PersonalTaskDto>            _openPersonal = new();
    private List<PersonalTaskDto>            _donePersonal = new();
    private List<PersonalTaskDto>            _visiblePersonal = new();

    /// <summary>Server-computed counts, so the tab badges and the section
    /// headings cannot drift apart or disagree with the daily digest.</summary>
    private MentorAttentionCountsDto Counts => _ws.Attention.Counts;

    /// <summary>Waiting phrase for the request currently open in the modal,
    /// taken from the same attention item the row rendered.</summary>
    private string? OpenRequestWaitingLabel =>
        _openRequestId is int id
            ? _awaitingMe.FirstOrDefault(r => r.EntityId == id)?.WaitingLabel
            : null;

    private Section? _focus;
    private bool     _personalExpanded;
    private int?     _openRequestId;
    private int?     _togglingId;

    private bool    _taskModalOpen;

    /// <summary>Null while creating, the task instance while editing. Handed
    /// straight to the shared modal, which owns all form state.</summary>
    private PersonalTaskDto? _editingTask;

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        Nav.LocationChanged += OnLocationChanged;
        ApplyFocusFromQuery();
        await ReloadAsync();

        // AFTER the load: the calendar links here with ?editTask={id}, and the
        // editor can only be seeded once that task's data actually exists.
        OpenTaskFromQuery();
    }

    public void Dispose() => Nav.LocationChanged -= OnLocationChanged;

    /// <summary>Home's two action tiles are ordinary links carrying ?focus=.
    /// Blazor reuses this component across such a navigation, so the query has
    /// to be re-read on LocationChanged as well as on init.</summary>
    private void OnLocationChanged(object? sender, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Routing.LocationChangedEventArgs e)
    {
        ApplyFocusFromQuery();
        InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);
    }

    /// <summary>One query value by name, or null. Hand-rolled because this
    /// project does not reference Microsoft.AspNetCore.WebUtilities — one
    /// shape, no parser dependency.</summary>
    private string? QueryValue(string key)
    {
        var query = new Uri(Nav.Uri).Query.TrimStart('?');

        foreach (var pair in query.Split('&', StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries))
        {
            var eq = pair.IndexOf('=');
            if (eq <= 0) continue;
            if (!pair.AsSpan(0, eq).Equals(key, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)) continue;
            return Uri.UnescapeDataString(pair[(eq + 1)..]);
        }

        return null;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Opens the editor for ?editTask={id}, the calendar's personal-task link.
    ///
    /// <para>Looks the id up in the list this mentor just loaded, so it can only
    /// ever open one of their OWN tasks — an id belonging to someone else simply
    /// is not found and nothing opens. No extra fetch and no second modal.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private void OpenTaskFromQuery()
    {
        if (!int.TryParse(QueryValue("editTask"), out var wantedId)) return;

        var task = _openPersonal.Concat(_donePersonal).FirstOrDefault(t => t.Id == wantedId);
        if (task is null) return;

        OpenEditTask(task);
    }

    private void ApplyFocusFromQuery() => _focus = FromSlug(QueryValue("focus"));

    private async Task ReloadAsync()
    {
        _loading = true;
        _ws = await Workspace.LoadAsync();

        // Both queues arrive filtered, aged and ordered worst-first. The three
        // things this method used to do — pick the awaiting-mentor status, sort
        // by timestamp, and let each row decide its own urgency — are all the
        // server's job now.
        _reviews    = _ws.Reviews;
        _awaitingMe = _ws.AwaitingMe;

        SplitPersonal(_ws.PersonalTasks);
        _loading = false;
    }

    private void SplitPersonal(IEnumerable<PersonalTaskDto> all)
    {
        _openPersonal = all.Where(t => !t.IsDone)
                           .OrderBy(t => t.DueDate ?? DateTime.MaxValue)
                           .ToList();
        _donePersonal = all.Where(t => t.IsDone)
                           .OrderByDescending(t => t.CreatedAt)
                           .ToList();
        RebuildVisiblePersonal();
    }

    /// <summary>Collapsed shows open tasks only, capped. Expanded appends the
    /// completed ones — the design keeps them reachable but never lets them
    /// push live work below the fold.</summary>
    private void TogglePersonalExpanded()
    {
        _personalExpanded = !_personalExpanded;
        RebuildVisiblePersonal();
    }

    private void RebuildVisiblePersonal() =>
        _visiblePersonal = _personalExpanded
            ? _openPersonal.Concat(_donePersonal).ToList()
            : _openPersonal.Take(PersonalCollapsedCount).ToList();

    // ── Filtering ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private bool Shows(Section s) => _focus is null || _focus == s;

    /// <summary>True while the wide column has anything to draw. False only
    /// under the משימות אישיות filter, which is also the one case where the
    /// workspace collapses to a single track — see <see cref="WorkspaceClass"/>.</summary>
    private bool ShowsPrimary => Shows(Section.Reviews) || Shows(Section.Requests);

    /// <summary>
    /// The two-column row is the "הכל" composition. Every filter leaves exactly
    /// one column standing, and a two-track grid with one empty track is a
    /// half-width panel beside bare canvas — so the row goes single-track
    /// instead and the surviving panel takes the full width.
    /// </summary>
    private string WorkspaceClass => _focus is null ? "" : "mt-workspace-solo";

    /// <summary>
    /// A panel in the wide column with nothing in it sizes to its own empty
    /// state instead of claiming half the column.
    ///
    /// <para>The student screen states the same rule by not rendering its
    /// attention band at all when empty, which lets משימות הפרויקט take the
    /// whole column. These two panels cannot simply vanish — an empty
    /// "אין הגשות לבדיקה כרגע" is a real answer to "what is waiting on me" and
    /// the reference keeps it — so they shrink rather than disappear, and the
    /// sibling grows into the space. Same outcome, one edge still shared.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private static string QuietWhenEmpty(int count) => count == 0 ? "mt-pane-quiet" : "";


    /// <summary>The pill group's four tabs. Each badge is the count its KPI
    /// card used to carry, and a zero renders no badge at all.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<MFilterTabs.Tab> FilterTabs => new[]
    {
        new MFilterTabs.Tab("",         "הכל"),
        new MFilterTabs.Tab("reviews",  "הגשות לבדיקה",   Counts.PendingSubmissions),
        new MFilterTabs.Tab("requests", "בקשות",          Counts.AwaitingRequests),
        new MFilterTabs.Tab("personal", "משימות אישיות",  _openPersonal.Count),
    };

    private string ActiveTabKey => _focus is null ? "" : Slug(_focus.Value);

    /// <summary>Selecting is not toggling: "הכל" is what clears.</summary>
    private void SelectFocus(string key) => _focus = FromSlug(key);

    private static string Slug(Section s) => s switch
    {
        Section.Reviews  => "reviews",
        Section.Requests => "requests",
        _                => "personal",
    };

    /// <summary>The inverse of <see cref="Slug"/>, and the single reader of the
    /// ?focus= vocabulary. An unrecognised value means "no filter" rather than
    /// an empty page.</summary>
    private static Section? FromSlug(string? value) => (value ?? "").ToLowerInvariant() switch
    {
        "reviews"  => Section.Reviews,
        "requests" => Section.Requests,
        "personal" => Section.Personal,
        _          => null,
    };

    // ── Rows ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// The row's whole second line: one short label for the team.
    ///
    /// <para>TeamName first, and the project only as a fallback. Project titles
    /// here are the long formal ones ("Motiva — Final Project Management
    /// Platform") while a team name is what a mentor actually recognises, so
    /// naming both put the long string on every row to add the short one. The
    /// milestone, the submitter and the request type left this line entirely —
    /// they are still on the item, and the detail surface each row opens is
    /// where they are read.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private static string TeamLabel(MentorAttentionItemDto i) =>
        !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(i.TeamName)     ? i.TeamName!
        : !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(i.ProjectTitle) ? i.ProjectTitle!
        : "";

    /// <summary>The same short line for a personal task, whose DTO carries the
    /// pair under different names. Empty when the task has no project — an
    /// unassigned reminder just has no second line.</summary>
    private static string PersonalTeamLabel(PersonalTaskDto t) =>
        !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(t.TeamName)     ? t.TeamName!
        : !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(t.ProjectTitle) ? t.ProjectTitle!
        : "";

    /// <summary>The row's state, in two words. The full WaitingLabel sentence
    /// is untouched on the DTO and is still what the request modal and the
    /// daily digest print — this is only what the scannable list shows.</summary>
    private static string StateLabel(MentorAttentionItemDto i) =>
        MentorAging.ShortLabel(i.WaitingDays);

    /// <summary>
    /// The waiting age, as the dashboard's TIME CHIP rather than as coloured
    /// text in the meta slot.
    ///
    /// <para>בית draws every deadline, waiting age and overdue duration on a
    /// small pill — `.mh-task-due` and `.mh-attn-time-late` — and this screen
    /// was drawing the same values as free-standing rose text. Same
    /// information, two visual languages; the dashboard is the reference, so
    /// the pill wins. It is <c>MStatusBadge</c> at
    /// <c>BadgeSize.Small</c>, which is that pill's metrics extracted into the
    /// shared primitive, so the two screens cannot draw it at two sizes.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>Tone is the SAME mapping the row's own MStatusBar already uses,
    /// so the bar and the chip on one row can never disagree: rose once the
    /// item has escalated, blue — the "waiting / in flight" role — before
    /// that. Rose ONLY at NEEDS ATTENTION; a NEW item must not read as an
    /// alarm.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private RenderFragment TimeChip(MentorAttentionItemDto i) => @<MStatusBadge
        Size="MStatusBadge.BadgeSize.Small"
        Variant="@(i.Age == MentorAttentionAge.NeedsAttention
                   ? MStatusBadge.BadgeVariant.Rose
                   : MStatusBadge.BadgeVariant.Info)"
        Text="@StateLabel(i)" />;

    /// <summary>
    /// A personal task's deadline, on the same chip.
    ///
    /// <para>The four states are בית's own, class for class
    /// (MentorHomePage.razor:960-963): an undated task shows NO chip rather
    /// than an empty one, a finished task goes neutral — done beats late, a
    /// completed task is not still overdue — an overdue one is rose, and
    /// anything else (יעד היום · יעד מחר · בעוד N ימים) takes the blue the
    /// dashboard gives every dated-and-not-late task.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private RenderFragment? DueChip(PersonalTaskDto t)
    {
        var label = MentorTime.DeadlineLabel(t.DueDate);
        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(label)) return null;

        var variant =
            t.IsDone                          ? MStatusBadge.BadgeVariant.Neutral
            : MentorTime.IsOverdue(t.DueDate) ? MStatusBadge.BadgeVariant.Rose
            :                                   MStatusBadge.BadgeVariant.Info;

        return @<MStatusBadge Size="MStatusBadge.BadgeSize.Small"
                              Variant="@variant"
                              Text="@label" />;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The row's urgency marker — <b>MStatusBar, not MStatusDot</b>.
    ///
    /// <para>These two feeds and the בית dashboard's דורש את תשומת לבך card
    /// render the SAME MentorAttentionItemDto out of the SAME
    /// IMentorWorkspaceService, and were drawing it two different ways: a
    /// 4×40 coloured bar there, an 8px dot here. One model, one marker — the
    /// bar, because the dashboard is the design source and the bar is what it
    /// draws. See Components/StatusBar for why the dot is still right on
    /// פרויקטים בהנחייתי and בקשות.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>Rose ONLY at NEEDS ATTENTION — a NEW item must not read as an
    /// alarm. The unescalated tone is blue rather than the violet the dot
    /// used, which is the dashboard's own choice for the same state and the
    /// finished palette's "in progress / waiting" role. Nothing about WHEN a
    /// row escalates changed: <c>MentorAttentionAge</c> arrives already set by
    /// GET /api/mentor/attention.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private static MStatusBar.BarTone BarToneFor(MentorAttentionItemDto i) =>
        i.Age == MentorAttentionAge.NeedsAttention
            ? MStatusBar.BarTone.Rose
            : MStatusBar.BarTone.Blue;

    /// <summary>The row's accessible name, with the escalation stated in words.
    ///
    /// <para>The reference's collapsed row carries its state as a coloured time
    /// phrase and a coloured dot, and both are visual. MentorAging's shared
    /// "דורש תשומת לב" is prepended here so an escalated row announces WHY it is
    /// escalated — colour is never the only carrier of that meaning.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private static string RowAriaLabel(MentorAttentionItemDto i, string action)
    {
        var state = MentorAging.StateLabel(i.Age);
        return state is null ? action : $"{state} — {action}";
    }

    // ── Personal task actions ───────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task ToggleTaskAsync(int id)
    {
        _togglingId = id;
        var ok = await PersonalTasks.ToggleAsync(id);
        _togglingId = null;

        if (!ok) return;

        // Flip locally rather than refetching the whole workspace: the toggle
        // endpoint answers a bool, and re-running four GETs to learn one bit
        // would make a checkbox feel like a page load.
        var all = _openPersonal.Concat(_donePersonal).ToList();
        var hit = all.FirstOrDefault(t => t.Id == id);
        if (hit is not null) hit.IsDone = !hit.IsDone;
        SplitPersonal(all);
    }

    private void OpenNewTask()
    {
        _editingTask   = null;
        _taskModalOpen = true;
    }

    private void OpenEditTask(PersonalTaskDto task)
    {
        _editingTask   = task;
        _taskModalOpen = true;
    }

    private void CloseTaskModal()
    {
        _taskModalOpen = false;
        _editingTask   = null;
    }

    /// <summary>Create or update finished. The modal already mirrored an edit
    /// onto the instance it was given, so an update just needs re-splitting;
    /// a create is appended.</summary>
    private void OnTaskSaved(PersonalTaskDto saved)
    {
        var all = _openPersonal.Concat(_donePersonal).ToList();

        if (!all.Any(t => t.Id == saved.Id)) all.Add(saved);

        SplitPersonal(all);
        _taskModalOpen = false;
        _editingTask   = null;
    }

    private void OnTaskDeleted(int deletedId)
    {
        SplitPersonal(_openPersonal.Concat(_donePersonal).Where(t => t.Id != deletedId));
        _taskModalOpen = false;
        _editingTask   = null;
    }
}
